- [Kelly] It's brilliant, I love it.

00:07:50.910 --> 00:07:51.960
- Thank you for watching it by the way.

00:07:51.960 --> 00:07:53.880
- I begged for it.

00:07:53.880 --> 00:07:55.207
Because, literally, I was like,

00:07:55.207 --> 00:07:57.180
"Am I gonna get to screen
this before I interview them?"

00:07:57.180 --> 00:07:58.410
I was, like, so excited.

00:07:58.410 --> 00:07:59.580
So I loved though,

00:07:59.580 --> 00:08:02.550
I was telling you when we were rehearsing,

00:08:02.550 --> 00:08:05.820
I loved how it's, like, dark,
but has a really great story,

00:08:05.820 --> 00:08:07.470
but also has this certain level of humor

00:08:07.470 --> 00:08:10.140
that's very cool and unique to your cast.

00:08:10.140 --> 00:08:12.000
- Yes.
- Your chemistry is amazing.

00:08:12.000 --> 00:08:13.590
Like, whoever did all the casting.

00:08:13.590 --> 00:08:14.423
- Yes.

00:08:14.423 --> 00:08:15.330
- It's like this odd bunch of people

00:08:15.330 --> 00:08:16.980
that I just never thought
I'd see in a film.

00:08:16.980 --> 00:08:18.690
And I was like, "This works so well."

00:08:18.690 --> 00:08:21.600
- It's a diverse group
that comes together.

00:08:21.600 --> 00:08:23.940
We got great chemistry,
when you guys see the movie.

00:08:23.940 --> 00:08:26.190
And we wanted to balance,

00:08:26.190 --> 00:08:29.670
the tricky thing I think with
Black Adam is he's darker,

00:08:29.670 --> 00:08:34.440
he's more intense, he's an
anti-hero, he's full of rage.

00:08:34.440 --> 00:08:36.540
He was a slave 5,000 years ago.

00:08:36.540 --> 00:08:38.010
His family was enslaved.

00:08:38.010 --> 00:08:38.843
- [Kelly] Mm-hmm.

00:08:38.843 --> 00:08:40.260
- His family was wiped away.

00:08:40.260 --> 00:08:42.810
And that's his drive and his rage.

00:08:42.810 --> 00:08:46.320
And what I always found
cool is Black Adam has

00:08:46.320 --> 00:08:49.427
all the superpowers of Superman.

00:08:49.427 --> 00:08:51.270
- But, like, more.

00:08:51.270 --> 00:08:53.610
- Well, Superman's greatest weakness

00:08:53.610 --> 00:08:55.350
is magic and kryptonite,

00:08:55.350 --> 00:08:57.780
and Black Adam's, one of
his superpowers is magic.

00:08:57.780 --> 00:08:58.770
So-

00:08:58.770 --> 00:09:00.163
- Boom, boom, mic drop!

00:09:00.163 --> 00:09:01.279
(Dwayne laughing)

00:09:01.279 --> 00:09:02.850
- [Dwayne] Boom boom!
- Boom boom!

00:09:02.850 --> 00:09:05.010
It's so good, it's so good.

00:09:05.010 --> 00:09:07.260
You're always very proud
of both of your cultures

00:09:07.260 --> 00:09:09.000
which I think is so important.

00:09:09.000 --> 00:09:10.122
Can you talk a little bit about that?

00:09:10.122 --> 00:09:10.955
- Yeah.

00:09:10.955 --> 00:09:12.510
- I don't know much
about the Samoan culture,

00:09:12.510 --> 00:09:13.830
so I think it's cool
that you teach people.

00:09:13.830 --> 00:09:15.260
- Yeah, absolutely.

00:09:15.260 --> 00:09:17.340
I'm half black and half Samoan.

00:09:17.340 --> 00:09:21.283
And recently on the Samoan side,

00:09:24.090 --> 00:09:28.230
I was, well just raised, I
was raised mainly in Hawaii

00:09:28.230 --> 00:09:29.310
and throughout the islands.

00:09:29.310 --> 00:09:30.780
And there's a term that we have in

00:09:30.780 --> 00:09:33.690
the islands called "mana"
which is like spirit and power.

00:09:33.690 --> 00:09:35.430
It like grounds us.

00:09:35.430 --> 00:09:39.510
That you could feel now between
us, ancestors, et cetera.

00:09:39.510 --> 00:09:41.370
So every time I go back to Hawaii,

00:09:41.370 --> 00:09:43.950
it's always very special
just to spend time there,

00:09:43.950 --> 00:09:44.850
spend time at the ocean.

00:09:44.850 --> 00:09:46.740
I love taking our little girls there.

00:09:46.740 --> 00:09:48.540
- Yeah.
- And getting that mana

00:09:48.540 --> 00:09:51.990
seeped in their blood
so to speak, you know?

00:09:51.990 --> 00:09:53.533
- Is it like a spiritual
energy kind of thing?

00:09:53.533 --> 00:09:56.010
- It is, so, it's like a
mana, like, you could feel it.

00:09:56.010 --> 00:09:57.150
It's kinda like when we come out,

00:09:57.150 --> 00:09:59.763
the mana is real in this
room and it's very positive.

00:09:59.763 --> 00:10:00.596
- Yeah.
- You know?

00:10:00.596 --> 00:10:02.730
And it can vibrate in a great way, so-

00:10:02.730 --> 00:10:04.350
- And when someone comes
in with some negative mana-

00:10:04.350 --> 00:10:05.499
- You can feel it.
- You're like "Um, bye!"

00:10:05.499 --> 00:10:06.332
- Yeah. (laughing)

00:10:06.332 --> 00:10:07.350
You can feel it, yeah.

00:10:07.350 --> 00:10:09.060
So it's a very powerful thing.

00:10:09.060 --> 00:10:10.920
And, yeah, so every time we go back

00:10:10.920 --> 00:10:14.550
it's always great to
introduce our daughters

00:10:14.550 --> 00:10:17.100
to their cultures.
- Yeah.

00:10:17.100 --> 00:10:20.490
- They are, let's see, our
daughters are part black,

00:10:20.490 --> 00:10:24.600
part Samoan, part Armenian, part Italian.

00:10:24.600 --> 00:10:26.430
So there's a lot going on
with our daughters, yeah.

00:10:26.430 --> 00:10:27.263
- Yeah-

00:10:27.263 --> 00:10:28.590
- That's a rad melting pot, though.

00:10:28.590 --> 00:10:30.140
- [Dwayne] It's great.
- Yeah.

